--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SURFACE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DateRangeFilter is the web inline date-range picker (web/src/components/forms/DateRangeFilter.tsx). The
web component renders a translucent pill holding a leading calendar glyph, a start <input type="date">,
a "->" separator and an end <input type="date">; an optional primary Apply button (rendered only when
an onApply handler is supplied); and an optional quick-select preset chip row (web DatePresetChips,
rendered by default - presets=true). The active preset is highlighted via matchPresetId(startDate,
endDate) matched against the WHOLE preset catalogue (web/src/lib/datePresets.ts), so a window matching a
preset that is not in the visible chip set highlights no chip. Choosing a chip resolves a concrete range
relative to "today" and either writes it atomically (web onRangeChange -> useUrlBatch's single
setBatch({from,to})) or fires the two granular setters (onStartDateChange + onEndDateChange), then calls
onApply?.().

Data sources (web): useTranslation (the i18n facade) and useUrlBatch (the atomic range writer). NEITHER
is a data fetch, so the web source has NO loading / empty / error / stale / offline branches to
reproduce - fabricating that chrome would be parity drift (the BulkActionsToolbar / VisuallyHidden
presentational-surface precedent). The branches the web source ACTUALLY has are reproduced in full and
verified headlessly: preset row shown vs hidden (web {presets && ...}), Apply shown vs hidden
(web {onApply && ...}), a chip active vs none (web activeId), the atomic-range vs two-granular-setter
selection path (web onRangeChange ? ... : ...), a custom preset subset (web presetIds, rendered in
catalogue order exactly as web DATE_PRESETS.filter), and an empty / malformed date window (web unset
input -> no active preset).

Native decomposition (the shipped 4-file shared-surface pattern):
  - DateRangeFilter.Model.cs      Registration (Slug "DateRangeFilter"; translation.* keys + English
                                  fallbacks for date.range.start/end/apply + date.preset.label, plus the
                                  preset-key helper that prefixes each catalogue key); DateRangeSelection
                                  (web onRangeChange {start,end}); DatePresetChip projection; PII-safe
                                  DateRangeFilterDiagnostics (view.opened slug=DateRangeFilter).
  - DateRangeFilter.Source.cs     IDateRangeUrlWriter (the useUrlBatch atomic-setter seam) + the inert
                                  no-op and recording doubles; IsoDate (yyyy-MM-dd parse/format, the web
                                  <input type=date> / iso() contract).
  - DateRangeFilter.ViewModel.cs  DateRangeFilterViewModel - the UI-thread-free state holder: controlled
                                  StartDate/EndDate, ShowPresets, HasApply, PresetIds, Today anchor,
                                  ActiveId (DatePresets.Match over the whole catalogue), Chips projection
                                  (catalogue order filtered to the visible ids), ChipVariantFor
                                  (active->Primary / inactive->Subtle for web primary/ghost),
                                  SetStartDate/SetEndDate (always forward + re-project), SelectPreset
                                  (atomic vs granular routing + onApply), RequestApply, events.
  - DateRangeFilter.cs            DateRangeFilter : ContentControl - the tokenized pill (SurfaceGlass bg
                                  + Border ring), a leading calendar FontIcon, two CalendarDatePickers
                                  bridged to ISO strings, the "->" separator, the optional primary Apply
                                  TsButton and the optional row of primary/subtle TsButton chips; binds
                                  every label/flag from the view-model, marshals changes to the UI thread,
                                  carries accessible names on every interactive element + a named Group
                                  automation peer, and emits view.opened once on Loaded.

Reuse (no atomic-component duplication): TeslaSync.App.Core.Forms.DatePresets / DatePreset / DateRange
(preset resolve + Match + DefaultIds + the 11-entry catalogue), ILocalizer / PassthroughLocalizer
(P1/S10), ButtonVariant / ControlSize (P1/S9), and the shared TsButton primitive (web @/components/ui/Button).

The interface member IDateRangeUrlWriter.WriteRange(string,string)'s second parameter was named endDate
(not end) because CA1716 (reserved VB keyword 'End') is an error under the app project's
TreatWarningsAsErrors - the same precedent as IGlobalProgressTicker.StopTicking in the 0141 sibling.

